@segment 26-28 Wetlands II
@start-level 26
# Added 2026-11-11 from the Questie audit (tools/questie_near.py): 98209 Bloom of the Heavens (1200 XP) is taken; it is handed in on the next Auberdine landing.
# Skyborne Mage. Same quests, order, hearth bind and flight paths as the Skyborne Druid segment 10 (Dwarf segment 09).
# Carry-in: 57/67/157/181/240/453 (Duskwood and Westfall, segment 11), 275/295/471 (Wetlands, done here),
# 1026 (Ashenvale, segment 13).
# Carry-out: 57, 67, 157, 181, 240, 453 (segment 11), 293 + 98190 (Stormwind, segment 11), 472 + 98223 (segment 12),
# 1026 (segment 13).
# Changes from the druid source:
# - Every combat hint rewritten for a mage of level 26-28 (Polymorph on the second raptor, Counterspell on casters,
#   Frost Nova / Blink / Cone of Cold to keep the hard hitters off you). Polymorph is only named for beasts; for the
#   cursed crew the hint says to fall back on Frost Nova if they are immune (their creature type is not in the data).
# - Training: the segment ends in Ironforge like the druid's and the Dwarf's, and a mage CAN train there. Added at
#   the end: `N Learn Teleport: Ironforge` at Milstaff Stormeye (tick it if an earlier Ironforge visit already
#   taught it) and `TRAIN` at Bink in the Hall of Mysteries (level 26 / 28).
# - No mage teleport is used for travel here: the Hearthstone is needed twice inside the segment (Menethil Harbor,
#   end of loop A and end of loop B), so there is no Teleport: Stormwind training trip, and the ending keeps the
#   druid's Hearthstone-or-walk to Menethil Harbor plus the gryphon to Ironforge. The step only mentions that a
#   mage who already knows Teleport: Ironforge can cast it from the catapult instead.
# - The mage walks: no mount yet.
@carry 57,67,157,161,181,240,275,295,453,471,1026
@done 277,294,484,98189

# ---------- Menethil Harbor ----------
S Menethil Harbor @ Wetlands, 10.7, 60.9 | You step off the boat from Auberdine. Bind at the Deepwater Tavern (Innkeeper Helbrek): you hearth back here after the first loop
A 473 | Valstag Ironjaw, in front of Menethil Keep (10.1,56.9)
T 473 | Captain Stoutfist, inside Menethil Keep
A 464 | Captain Stoutfist
A 98221 @ Wetlands, 9.9, 57.4 | Captain Stoutfist (new in Forever)
A 98230 | Captain Stoutfist (new in Forever): a walk to Howin Kindfeather, far east along the road
A 98190 @ Wetlands, 9.9, 57.4 | Captain Stoutfist (new in Forever). The Menethil Statuette goes to Stormwind Keep in the next segment: keep it in your bags
A 472 | Harlo Barnaby (10.8,55.9). Needs level 25. Just a walk to Dun Modr: you hand it in in segment 12
A 98208 @ Wetlands, 8.0, 55.9 | Sylessa Duskwhisper (new in Forever), near the tanner. Her flower is in the wreck south of town: you get it after the first loop
A 288 | First Mate Fitzsimmons, by the docks
C 288 @ Wetlands, 10.7, 60.9 | Buy a Flagon of Mead from Innkeeper Helbrek in the Deepwater Tavern
T 288 | First Mate Fitzsimmons
A 289 | First Mate Fitzsimmons

# ---------- Loop A, part 1: crocolisks and the cursed crew ----------
C 471 @ Wetlands, 19.0, 25.0 | Leave by the bridge and go north along the coast. Giant Wetlands Crocolisks (25-26) swim in the river mouths at 15-27,19-29, next to the shipwrecks. Kill until you have 6 skins. Fen Creepers (24-25, stealthed in the water at 18-24,27-32) count for Blisters on the Land: kill the ones you meet
C 289 @ Wetlands, 14.3, 26.9 | The two wrecks on the north coast (13-16,23-31). Cursed Sailors (26-27) are mostly around the southern wreck, Cursed Marines (27-28) around the northern one; First Mate Snellig (29) stands in the southern wreck at 13.8,30.2. They come in twos: Polymorph the second one (if it is immune, Frost Nova both and step back), drink between pulls. Clear around Snellig first, then fight him with full mana
T 471 @ Wetlands, 8.5, 55.7 | Walk back to Menethil Harbor. James Halloran, the tanner
A 98072 @ Wetlands, 8.5, 55.8 | James Halloran (new in Forever). The whelps are far to the east; you get them at the end of this loop
T 289 | First Mate Fitzsimmons
A 290 | First Mate Fitzsimmons

# ---------- Loop A, part 2: the strongbox, Whelgar's dig, Angerfang ----------
C 290 @ Wetlands, 15.4, 23.6 | Back north to the far (northern) wreck. Captain Halyndor (30) stands on it at 15.4,23.6 with Marines around him. Pull the Marines away one at a time first; keep Halyndor off you: Frostbolt from maximum range, Frost Nova when he reaches you, Blink away and go on casting; Mana Shield if your health gets low. He drops the Intrepid Strongbox Key
T 290 | Intrepid's Locked Strongbox, in the same wreck (14.4,24.0)
A 292 | The same strongbox
A 299 | Go south-east across the marsh to Whelgar's Excavation Site (stay north of the road until you are past the murloc coast). Prospector Whelgar stands at the camp on the east rim of the dig (38.8,52.4)
C 295,299 @ Wetlands, 34.0, 48.0 | Down in the dig (31-36,44-52): kill 10 Mottled Scytheclaws and 10 Mottled Razormaws (25-27) and pick up the four tablet fragments. Ados, Modr and Golm are in Ancient Relics (stone tablets), Neru is in a Loose Soil mound; they sit in different spots each time, so check 34.1,49.9 / 35.2,51.5 / 34.2,47.7 / 33.1,46.4 and the north end around 34.3,44.5 and 36.5,42.1. Raptors pull in pairs: Polymorph one of them to split them
T 295 | Ormer Ironbraid, next to Whelgar
A 296 | Ormer Ironbraid
C 296 @ Wetlands, 33.3, 51.5 | Sarltooth (29) is at the south-west side of the dig (33.3,51.5). Clear the raptors near him first. Frostbolt from maximum range, Frost Nova when he reaches you, step back or Blink and go on casting; Cone of Cold slows him too. Do not let him stay on you: he hits hard for your level
T 296 | Ormer Ironbraid
T 299 | Prospector Whelgar
C 98221:1 @ Wetlands, 38.6, 46.1 | Go north-east. The first set of Attack Plans lies at the small Dragonmaw post west of the Angerfang Encampment (38.6,46.1). Click it to destroy it. Which of the four plans lies where is not in the data: if this spot is empty, go on and tick it later
C 464,98221 @ Wetlands, 45.5, 44.5 | Angerfang Encampment (39-52,40-49). Any Dragonmaw drops War Banners (8 needed): Raiders (26-27) and Bonewarders (27, casters: Counterspell their casts). The other Attack Plans are at about 45.5,42.6, 45.3,45.5 and 49.4,46.6. Fight at the edges, one tent at a time; the Dragonmaw Battlemaster (rare, 30) walks the middle: avoid him. Leave the catapults for the next loop
T 98230 @ Wetlands, 49.4, 42.1 | Howin Kindfeather, just north of the encampment beside the road (49.4,42.1)
A 98246 @ Wetlands, 49.4, 42.1 | Howin Kindfeather (new in Forever). The eggs come from Raptor Ridge in the next loop. If he does not offer it yet, he will after Razormaw Needling in loop B
C 275 @ Wetlands, 54.5, 41.0 | Finish the 8 Fen Creepers in the water around Rethiel's island (53-55,36-46); they are stealthed until you are close
T 275 | Rethiel the Greenwarden (56.4,40.4)
C 98072 @ Wetlands, 61.0, 40.0 | Crimson Whelps (25-26) fly over the Green Belt east of Rethiel (57-70,31-51). Collect 10 Pristine Crimson Scales. Their fire bolt is a cast: Counterspell stops it and Fire Ward takes some of it. Polymorph does not work on whelps: pull one at a time. Stay north of the orcs in the hills
A 98223 @ Wetlands, 53.5, 54.5 | Go south-west to the Dragonmaw camp south of the road. The Tattered Spellbook lies on the ground at 53.5,54.5 (new in Forever). Dragonmaw Centurions and Shadowwarders (28-29) stand around it: pull one at a time, Counterspell the Shadowwarders' casts, and finish your 8 War Banners here if you are short. You keep this quest until segment 12
H Menethil Harbor | Hearthstone back to Menethil Harbor

# ---------- Menethil Harbor hand-ins ----------
T 464 | Captain Stoutfist
A 465 | Captain Stoutfist. Do not take Defeat Nek'rosh later: it is an elite fight
T 98221 @ Wetlands, 9.9, 57.4 | Captain Stoutfist. Keep Old Habits (98223) and A Friend of the Family (98190) in the log for later segments
T 98072 @ Wetlands, 8.5, 55.8 | James Halloran
A 98240 @ Wetlands, 8.5, 55.8 | James Halloran (new in Forever): a crate for Howin Kindfeather
T 292 | Glorin Steelbrow, at the Deepwater Tavern (10.6,60.6)
A 293 | Glorin Steelbrow. The eye goes to the Cathedral in Stormwind in the next segment
C 98208 @ Wetlands, 12.1, 64.2 | The wreck just south of town, across the water from the docks (about 12,64). Bluegill Raiders (28-29) live in and around it; kill them and search the wreck for Nord'el. Whether the flower drops or is picked up is not in the data: loot every murloc and click anything that sparkles. Pull one murloc at a time and Frost Nova the ones that run for help
T 98208 @ Wetlands, 8.0, 55.9 | Sylessa Duskwhisper.
A 98209 @ Wetlands, 8.0, 55.9 | Sylessa Duskwhisper: Bloom of the Heavens. Nord'el goes to Auberdine: you carry it until the next boat there

# ---------- Loop B: Howin Kindfeather and Raptor Ridge ----------
T 98240 @ Wetlands, 49.4, 42.1 | Follow the road east, past Whelgar's dig, to Howin Kindfeather (49.4,42.1)
A 98245 @ Wetlands, 49.4, 42.1 | Howin Kindfeather (new in Forever). Take Trying Times (98246) too if he only offers it now
C 98245,98246 @ Wetlands, 63.0, 30.5 | Raptor Ridge, north-east of Howin (58-72,22-40): Highland Razormaws (27-28) and Elder Razormaws (29) drop the 10 Razormaw Incisors and the 12 Perfect Razormaw Eggs (look for nests on the ground too; the data does not say whether the eggs drop or are picked up). Stay at the south and west edge: the Razormaw Matriarch (rare, 31) is deep inside at 70,29. Raptors come in pairs: Polymorph the second one
T 98245 @ Wetlands, 49.4, 42.1 | Howin Kindfeather
T 98246 @ Wetlands, 49.4, 42.1 | Howin Kindfeather. Ignore his follow-ups: they are group quests
T 465 | Cross the road into the Angerfang Encampment and click a Dragonmaw Catapult (47.5,47.0) to hand in. Do not take Defeat Nek'rosh (elite)

# ---------- Back to Menethil Harbor and on to Ironforge ----------
H Menethil Harbor | If the Hearthstone is ready again (you used it about an hour ago), hearth to Menethil Harbor. If not, walk the road west to Menethil Harbor and tick this step there. Already know Teleport: Ironforge? Cast it right here instead and press Skip on this step and on the flight
FLY Ironforge @ Wetlands, 9.5, 59.7 | Shellei Brondir, the gryphon master by the docks
N Learn Teleport: Ironforge @ Ironforge, 25.5, 7.1 | Milstaff Stormeye, the Portal Trainer in the Hall of Mysteries in the Mystic Ward (north-west of the city). Taught from level 20. Already know it? Tick this
TRAIN @ Ironforge, 27.3, 8.3 | Bink, the mage trainer a few steps away in the Hall of Mysteries: learn everything up to your level (Cone of Cold at 26, the level 28 spells if you are 28). Buy Runes of Teleportation from a reagent vendor until you carry 5 or more
N Segment done. In the log: 57, 67, 157, 181, 240, 453 (Duskwood/Westfall), 293 and 98190 (Stormwind), 472 and 98223 (segment 12), 1026 (Ashenvale) | Your hearthstone stays in Menethil Harbor
